            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-18T04:04:05Z",
            "count": 0,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "## Summary\n\n`toupper()` and `tolower()` accept UTF-8-marked strings holding overlong forms, which `validUTF8()` rejects: an overlong surrogate comes back as a 3-byte surrogate that R itself then refuses, an overlong NUL truncates the string, and on Linux each surrogate warns twice. Fixes a reproducible bug: wrong results, and an OSS-Fuzz timeout from the warnings.\n\n## Details\n\n`utf8toucs()` in `src/main/util.c` rejects surrogates only in its 3-byte branch, and no branch rejects overlong (non-shortest) forms, so `F0 8D BF B0` decodes to U+DFF0 and `C0 80` to NUL. On Linux, `wcstoutf8()` then warns \"unpaired surrogate Unicode point\" on both of its passes; the OSS-Fuzz input, 56 KB with 5941 such forms, raised 11882 warnings. Tested on R-devel r90925.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `utf8toucs-overlong-repro.R`; prints what `toupper()` returns for each form (re-encoded or truncated before the patch, an error after) and the warning count (10000 on Linux before, 0 after).\n\nProposed patch: attached as `utf8toucs-overlong.diff`; rejects overlong forms in every branch of `utf8toucs()`, so they give the usual \"invalid input\" error, and adds a test to `tests/reg-fuzz.R`.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/509, where CI results can be seen.",
            "bug_id": 19337
          },
